  "answer": "### Issue Presented\nA non-VAT-registered seller cannot issue a VAT invoice. Under Section 236 of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC), only VAT-registered persons are authorized to issue VAT invoices. This is further supported by Revenue Regulation No. 16-2005, which defines a \"VAT-registered person\" as someone registered as a VAT taxpayer under Section 236 of the NIRC.\n\nIn practical terms, if a seller is not registered for VAT, they must issue a regular sales invoice instead of a VAT invoice. This distinction is crucial for compliance and for the buyer's ability to claim input VAT.\n\n### Relevant Facts / Assumptions\nThe factual circumstances have not been fully described. The analysis is based on the question as presented.\n\n### Alternative Interpretations\nNo alternative interpretations identified from the available indexed authorities.\n\n### Position Strength\nPosition strength is preliminary and subject to full fact pattern verification.",
